.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
Provides a low-level bit window over a referenced ulong value\&. This type exposes individual bits as a mutable span-like view with support for forward, reverse, and ring-based indexing modes\&. 

\fBWarning:\fP This API is intended for advanced developers only\&. It operates directly on a referenced integer and mutates its bits without safety guards, bounds normalization, or copy-on-write semantics\&. Incorrect usage may lead to unexpected side effects, corrupted state, or infinite iteration when using ring mode\&. 

.PP
\fBref struct:\fP The type is stack-only and cannot be boxed, stored on the heap, captured by lambdas, or used in async methods\&. 

.PP
\fBDirect bit mutation:\fP All operations modify the underlying integer in-place\&. Multiple spans referencing the same integer will observe each other's changes\&. 

.PP
\fBWindowed view:\fP The span exposes only the bits between \fRStart\fP and \fREnd\fP\&. Access outside this range throws exceptions\&. 

.PP
\fBIndexing modes:\fP 
.PD 0
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBSystem\fP: forward indexing (Start → End)\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBReverse\fP: backward indexing (End-1 → Start)\&. 
.IP "\(bu" 2
\fBRing\fP: cyclic indexing; enumeration never terminates\&. 
.PP

